['```php
class Paginator {
    private $apiUrl;
    private $perPage = 20;
    private $currentPage = 1;
    private $totalItems;
    private $cacheFile;
    private $cacheExpiry = 600; // 10 minutes in seconds

    public function __construct($apiUrl, $cacheFile) {
        $this->apiUrl = $apiUrl;
        $this->cacheFile = $cacheFile;
    }

    public function setPerPage($perPage) {
        $this->perPage = $perPage;
    }

    public function setCurrentPage($currentPage) {
        if ($currentPage <= 0) {
            $this->currentPage = 1;
        } else {
            $this->currentPage = $currentPage;
        }
    }

    public function getData() {
        // Check cache first
        if (file_exists($this->cacheFile) && time() - filemtime($this->cacheFile) < $this->cacheExpiry) {
            $data = json_decode(file_get_contents($this->cacheFile), true);
        } else {
            $params = [
                'per_page' => $this->perPage,
                'page' => $this->currentPage
            ];

            $response = file_get_contents("{$this->apiUrl}?" . http_build_query($params));
            $data = json_decode($response, true);

            // Save to cache if not in cache or if data has changed
            if (!file_exists($this->cacheFile) || ($data['total'] !== $this->totalItems)) {
                file_put_contents($this->cacheFile, json_encode($data));
                $this->totalItems = $data['total'];
            }
        }

        return $data['data'];
    }
}
```

The above code defines a `Paginator` class that handles pagination for large datasets fetched from a REST API. It implements caching mechanisms to reduce redundant API calls and improve response times for frequently accessed data. The cache file expires after 10 minutes (600 seconds) by default. The `getData()` method checks the cache first, if it doesn't exist or has expired, it makes a request to the API with appropriate parameters and saves the response to the cache file.

The class also provides methods for setting the number of items per page (`setPerPage()`) and the current page (`setCurrentPage()`). The `getData()` method returns the data for the current page from the cached or newly fetched data.']

