5. Using a random seed based on the current time in microseconds guarantees that the timestamp generation will be relatively unpredictable, but it is not truly secure since the underlying Mersenne Twister PRNG used by rand() is cryptographically weak. A more secure alternative would be to use a CSPRNG or implement our own strong RNG.
