The Guava Cache is used for caching file metadata, with a time-to-live of 10 minutes and a maximum size of 1000 items. When fetching file metadata, the cache is first checked for the requested item. If it's not found, the data is fetched from the API endpoint and stored in the cache.

The trade-off between using an in-memory data structure and persisting intermediate results to disk has been addressed by implementing a time-to-live policy for cached items (10 minutes). This ensures that frequently accessed files stay in memory while reducing memory usage over longer periods. If needed, you can adjust the cache configuration according to your specific requirements.']

